---
import Files01DocumentImages from "../../components/Files01DocumentImages.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { shares, fileEvidence } from "../../data/fileCentre";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Company files" description="Explore the actual five shared departmental folders, identity-based access, DFS paths and permission checks." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Explore",href:"company/"},{label:"Files"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">Company files / Five departments</div>
  <h1>Company File Centre</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-top:18px">The Company File Centre is the central place where Nova Corp employees find their shared department folders. Each team has its own space, and access is controlled by company accounts.</p>
  <div class="button-row" style="margin-top:25px"><a class="btn" href={base+"files/shares/it/"}>Follow an IT employee's request →</a><a class="btn ghost" href={base+"files/dfs/"}>Understand the company file address</a></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
  <section class="content-section"><h2>Why does it exist?</h2><h3 class="file-problem">Problem</h3><p>Imagine <a href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Moyo</a> needs a support document but does not know which colleague or computer holds it. Even if she remembers a server name, a future storage move could change that address.</p><h3 class="file-solution">Solution</h3><p>The IT team created a company file address with one folder for each department. <a href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Moyo</a> can open her department drive and find the shared document without asking a colleague where it is stored. DFS locates the folder; Windows checks whether she is authorized to open it.</p><Files01DocumentImages ids={["dfs-namespace-gui","dfs-client-mapped-drive"]}/></section><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose a department</div><h2>Open a shared folder</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={base+"files/permissions/"}>Compare permissions →</a></div>
  <div class="area-grid">
  {shares.map((share,index)=><a class="area-card" href={base+"files/shares/"+share.id+"/"} style={"--accent:"+(share.id==="finance"?"#7C3AED":"#2563EB")}>
    <div class="number"><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")} / SHARED FOLDER</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div>
    <h3>{share.name}</h3><p>{share.purpose}</p>
    <span class="arrow-label">Follow access →</span>
  </a>)}
  </div>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:18px 0"><a href={base+"files/permissions/technical/"}>Need the exact Windows access entries? Explore the complete 100-rule technical permission browser →</a></p>
  <div class="grid-main" style="margin-top:30px">
    <div class="paper panel">
      <p class="kicker">Walkthrough / Document request</p>
      <h3 style="margin:12px 0 15px"><a href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Moyo</a> opens an IT team file.</h3>
      <p class="muted">Her IT account belongs to a department group, nested into a resource-permission group. A familiar DFS path leads to the real share, where Windows evaluates both share permissions and folder permissions.</p>
      <div class="button-row" style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn small" href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Start with Moyo →</a><a class="btn ghost small" href={base+"files/shares/it/"}>Open the IT share</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="paper panel">
      <p class="kicker">An important difference</p>
      <h3 style="margin:12px 0 15px">Finance has a second authorization path.</h3>
      <p class="muted">Finance staff use standard Modify permissions. Authorized management identities receive broader Finance FullControl through a separate nested group.</p>
      <a class="evidence-link" href={base+"files/shares/finance/"}>See why Finance is different →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section class="section soft-band"><div class="container">
 <h2>Three things that must not be confused</h2>
 <div class="outcome-grid">
   <div class="outcome"><strong>The company address</strong><p>The DFS namespace directs employees to one of five targets. The namespace's Read rule does not grant unrestricted access to departmental documents.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"files/dfs/"}>Follow DFS referrals →</a></div>
   <div class="outcome"><strong>Network vs folder rights</strong><p>SMB share permission and NTFS folder permission are evaluated separately. A working network connection is not enough to open a restricted file.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"files/permissions/"}>Compare both checks →</a></div>
   <div class="outcome"><strong>Backup vs earlier version</strong><p>Windows Backup restored a deleted file in one test; Shadow Copy preserved a previous version in another. Both have different limits.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"recovery/"}>See recovery options →</a></div>
 </div>
 <section class="content-section"><h2>Related tests and incidents</h2><p><a href={base+"incidents/file-permission-denial/"}>Controlled folder permission failure →</a></p><p><a href={base+"incidents/dns-client-outage/"}>Controlled DNS failure →</a></p><h2>Engineering journals</h2><p><a href={base+"journals/"}>Original CR-009 and CR-010 PDFs →</a></p></section><p class="source-line">The detailed access lists cover specified shares and folder levels, not every file recursively. <a href={fileEvidence.full}>Original engineering journal ↗</a></p>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>.file-problem{color:#edb4a2;margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem}.file-solution{color:#c6dcb4;margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem}.prose,.content-section{min-width:0}.prose pre{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;box-sizing:border-box}.content-section details{margin:16px 0}.content-section summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}</style>
